===Take the starskiff and enter Scalegorge Waterscape{{subst:void|<!--102120121-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location=Alchemy Commission|update|In a sudden turn of events, the master primus of the Disciples of Sanctus Medicus calls out on the brink of death for the one who brought the Stellaron to her, the assistant from the Antimatter Legion. Then, the guide who had been beside you all this time, "Miss Tingyun," suddenly turns into a ball of flame in a terrifying fashion, declaring to you their true identity of Phantylia, the Lord Ravager.<br />Phantylia uses the Legion's soldiers to block your path while moving deeper into Scalegorge Waterscape to claim the source of the Xianzhou natives' immortality &mdash; the Ambrosial Arbor.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
:'''Fu Xuan:''' We need to take a starskiff to Scalegorge Waterscape &mdash; the Ambrosial Arbor can be sealed from that delve.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' (Trailblazer), let's make haste.

;(Talk to Fu Xuan)
:'''Fu Xuan:''' That impostor had the audacity to carry out her nefarious plans right under our noses... How utterly despicable.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' What worries me more is... just how many more Antimatter saboteurs are at large?
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} About Tingyun...
::'''March 7th:''' It all happened so suddenly... but looking back, I think Mr. Yang was right. Tingyun was behaving strangely &mdash; she was fascinated with the Abundance's creations.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Since she was an Amicassador dispatched by the Sky-Faring Commission, it's evident that there must indeed be a person with her name in the Commission. We'll have to let the Cloud Knights get to the bottom of what happened to the real Tingyun.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' As for the "Tingyun" who accompanied us all that way, it's like what Mr. Yang said &mdash; her appearance was designed to sow seeds of doubt among us... we cannot allow ourselves to fall into her trap.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} About Scalegorge Waterscape...
::'''Fu Xuan:''' It is a delve governed by the Vidyadhara &mdash; supposedly an ancient oceanic region transferred from the Vidyadhara home planet.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' After the Ambrosial Arbor was broken in two during the war, its roots were left gnarled and broken... yet it never died.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' The Alliance decided to seal the Arbor within Scalegorge Waterscape, entrust it to the high elders of the Vidyadhara, and rely on the power of Long's Scions to constrain it.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' It has been so long &mdash; no one knows whether the seal remains... Even if it does, I doubt it will hinder that spectral Lord Ravager.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Where is Jing Yuan?
::'''Fu Xuan:''' I've reported the current situation to the Seat of Divine Foresight.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' He made no further contact after we communicated at the Matrix of Prescience. He said he had "important matters to personally attend to."
::'''Fu Xuan:''' The situation stands on the edge of a precipice. We must trust in the general...
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Time is of the essence. Let's go.
:<pre>{
	"$type": "RPG.GameCore.OpenTreasureChallenge",
	"RaidID": 40231001
}</pre>
:{{Диалог|Выход}} (Stay here for now.)
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Why are we still here? Things will change if we tarry too long.

;(Talk to Investigate)
:'''Recuperating Cloud Knight:''' Don't worry. I just took some medicine and the wound will heal up soon.
:'''March 7th:''' Yay, we did it! Can't see the smoke anymore.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' E&mdash;Excellent. I'll lead my troops to the rendezvous.
{{Dialogue End}}

